<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Salyes</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 123 BCE (approx.) · capital Entremont</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celto-Ligurian confederation inland of Marseille whose wars with Greek Massalia drew Rome into Gaul and led to the founding of Aix-en-Provence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Salyes were a league of Ligurian and Celtic communities in lower <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/var-river">Var</a>. Greek writers mention them from the 4th century BCE as troublesome neighbours of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Massalia</a>. Their chief stronghold was the oppidum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entremont-oppidum">Entremont</a> on a plateau north of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aix</a>, fortified in the 2nd century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entremont-oppidum">Entremont</a> is known for its stone sculptures of seated warriors and carved severed heads, and for a portico where real skulls were displayed, reflecting a warrior cult of the head. The Salyes farmed olives and cereals, pressed oil and traded with the Greek coast while raiding it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Massalia</a> appealed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>, and campaigns in 125 to 123 BCE under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-fulvius-flaccus-consul-125-bce">Marcus Fulvius Flaccus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-sextius-calvinus">Gaius Sextius Calvinus</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entremont-oppidum">Entremont</a>. Their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutomalius">Teutomalius</a> fled to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/allobroges">Allobroges</a>. In 122 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aquae Sextiae</a> (Aix-en-Provence) nearby, and the territory became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-narbonensis">Gallia Narbonensis</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 123 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:5.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 123 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Entremont</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Teutomalius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Salluvii, Salyens</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-262&amp;focus=salyes" aria-label="Salyes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4806 627 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Salyes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5126 883L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5126 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5126 883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-262&amp;focus=salyes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

